Output5[Expected Approach 1] Using Top-Down DP (Memoization) - O(sum*n) time and O(sum*n) spaceIn the previous recursive approach, we observed that many subproblems are solved repeatedly. This repetition increases time complexity. To handle this, we use Memoization.We create a DP table of size n × (sum + 1), because the result of the recursion depends on two changing parameters: the number of coins considered and the remaining target sum So whenever we compute a subproblem count(i, sum), we store the result in the DP table. Next time when the same subproblem appears, instead of computing it again, we directly fetch it from the DP table, which saves a lot of time.
